# meta-lastandfast

Lastandfast custom Yocto layer for the INAR robotic arm.
Target: NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano 8GB (jetson-orin-nano-devkit-nvme)

## Hardware

- Board: NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano 8GB Developer Kit Super
- Module: P3767-0005
- Carrier: P3768-0000
- Storage: NVMe SSD (M.2 2242)

## Software Stack

- OS: Lastandfast OS 1.0
- ROS 2: Humble
- CUDA: 12.6
- TensorRT: 10.3.0
- cuDNN: 9.3.0
- Cameras: Intel RealSense D435 (librealsense2), Orbbec Gemini 336L (OrbbecSDK)
- Python: 3.12 + NumPy + OpenCV

## Partition Layout

| Partition | Mount | Type | Mode |
|-----------|-------|------|------|
| NVMe slot A | / (slot A) | ext4 | read-only |
| NVMe slot B | / (slot B) | ext4 | read-only |
| /data | /data | ext4 | read-write |

## OTA Strategy

A/B partition scheme. Active slot selected by bootloader (CBoot/U-Boot).
Updates written to inactive slot. Rollback automatic on boot failure.
/etc/fstab uses /dev/root (bootloader-resolved) not hardcoded partition.

## Build Instructions

1. Install Yocto dependencies on Ubuntu 22.04:
   sudo apt install -y gawk wget git diffstat unzip texinfo gcc build-essential chrpath socat cpio python3 python3-pip python3-pexpect xz-utils debianutils iputils-ping python3-git python3-jinja2 python3-subunit zstd liblz4-tool file locales libacl1 gfortran

2. Clone layers:
   mkdir -p ~/lastandfast && cd ~/lastandfast
   git clone -b scarthgap https://git.yoctoproject.org/poky.git
   git clone -b scarthgap https://github.com/OE4T/meta-tegra.git
   git clone -b scarthgap https://github.com/openembedded/meta-openembedded.git
   git clone -b scarthgap https://github.com/ros/meta-ros.git
   git clone https://github.com/eldu-lastandfast/meta-lastandfast.git

3. Initialize build environment:
   source poky/oe-init-build-env build

4. Add layers:
   bitbake-layers add-layer ~/lastandfast/meta-openembedded/meta-oe
   bitbake-layers add-layer ~/lastandfast/meta-openembedded/meta-python
   bitbake-layers add-layer ~/lastandfast/meta-openembedded/meta-networking
   bitbake-layers add-layer ~/lastandfast/meta-openembedded/meta-initramfs
   bitbake-layers add-layer ~/lastandfast/meta-tegra
   bitbake-layers add-layer ~/lastandfast/meta-lastandfast
   bitbake-layers add-layer ~/lastandfast/meta-ros/meta-ros-common
   bitbake-layers add-layer ~/lastandfast/meta-ros/meta-ros2
   bitbake-layers add-layer ~/lastandfast/meta-ros/meta-ros2-humble

5. Configure local.conf:
   MACHINE = "jetson-orin-nano-devkit-nvme"
   ROS_DISTRO = "humble"
   ROS_OE_RELEASE_SERIES = "scarthgap"
   LICENSE_FLAGS_ACCEPTED = "commercial_cuda-binaries nvidia-sdk"
   IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " base-files lastandfast-users plymouth-lastandfast lastandfast-watchdog lastandfast-journald cuda-libraries cuda-cudart tensorrt-core cudnn ros-base librealsense2 orbbec-sdk python3-numpy python3-opencv inar-robot"

6. Build:
   bitbake core-image-minimal

## Flash Instructions

1. Install device-tree-compiler:
   sudo apt install -y device-tree-compiler

2. Put Jetson into recovery mode:
   - Unplug power
   - Short FC REC to GND
   - Plug power back in
   - Wait 2 seconds, remove jumper
   - Connect USB cable to PC

3. Attach USB to WSL:
   usbipd bind --busid X-X
   usbipd attach --wsl --busid X-X

4. Flash:
   cd ~/lastandfast/build/tmp/deploy/images/jetson-orin-nano-devkit-nvme
   tar xf core-image-minimal-jetson-orin-nano-devkit-nvme.rootfs.tegraflash.tar.gz
   sudo ./doflash.sh

## Adding a New Machine Target (e.g. Orin NX)

In conf/local.conf change:
MACHINE = "jetson-orin-nano-devkit-nvme"
to:
MACHINE = "jetson-orin-nx-devkit"

All recipes in meta-lastandfast are machine-agnostic and will work unchanged.

## Branding

- Hostname: inari
- Default user: inari
- OS name: Lastandfast OS 1.0 (INAR)
- Boot splash: Lastandfast Plymouth theme
- Shell prompt: [lastandfast@inari]
